=== live dry-run note ===

A live `kvkk-retention` dry-run against the running Compose stack was attempted
but not captured: the deployed/running Host image predates the wave-21 code, so
the container falls through to the generic usage text instead of dispatching the
new verb (it needs a Host image rebuilt from this commit).

The verb's full behavior is proven instead by `KvkkRetentionTests` (see
`kvkk-tests.log`, 3/3 passed) which exercises it end to end against a real
migrated PostgreSQL test database:

- dry-run (default): opens a transaction, counts each class
  (`staff=1 order_notes=1 item_notes=1 reservation_reasons=1 apply=false`),
  rolls back — DB unchanged.
- `--apply`: anonymizes exactly the past-retention rows; recent / active /
  wrong-status / legally-held (`--exclude-order-ids-file`) rows untouched.
- second `--apply`: reports all zeros (idempotent).
- missing `--db-url` / unknown argument: exit 2 (fail-closed).

After the next Host image rebuild, run:

    dotnet ALKAROS.Host.dll kvkk-retention --db-url postgresql://alkaros@postgres:5432/alkaros

and expect `kvkk-retention: staff=0 order_notes=0 item_notes=0 reservation_reasons=0 ... apply=false`
on the pilot database (every retention window is 1-5 years, so a fresh
deployment reports zeros for years).
